      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This an edited transcript of the Lee E. Farr Lecture given by Dr. Jeffrey Flier on May 8, 2012, at the culmination of the annual Student Research Day at the Yale School of Medicine. In this presentation, Dr. Flier discusses his and his wife's research on insulin, leptin, and FGF21 in the context of his reflections upon his life's work and his advice for young investigators."},
